        },
        "method_dtg": {
          "type": "method",
          "settings": {
            "name": "DTG",
            "description": "Best for detailed, photo-quality prints on cotton garments.",
            "details": "<p>Direct to Garment. The printer sprays water-based ink straight into the fibres of the shirt, the way an inkjet prints onto paper. The ink becomes part of the fabric rather than sitting on it.</p><p>That makes it the softest finish — you can barely feel the print — and the best choice for photographs and fine gradients. It needs cotton, and it prints richest on lighter garments.</p>",
            "best_for": "Photographs, fine detail and gradients, soft hand feel, 100% cotton"
          }
        },
        "method_emb": {
          "type": "method",
          "settings": {
            "name": "Embroidery",
            "description": "Best for a premium, textured look on hats, polos and jackets.",
            "details": "<p>Your design is stitched into the garment with thread rather than printed. The artwork is first digitised into a stitch file, then sewn by machine.</p><p>It gives a raised, textured, permanent finish that reads as premium, and it outlasts any print. Fine detail and small text do not stitch well, so simpler, bolder artwork works best.</p>",
